        "## Investigate Anomaly Impact\n",
        "\n",
        "### Subtask:\n",
        "Analyze how the identified abnormal pollution patterns (from the DBSCAN step) might affect the robustness of the prediction models. This could involve retraining models on cleaned data or using anomaly scores as features and comparing performance.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cdc35885"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I need to filter out the anomalies from `df_scaled` using the `dbscan_label_tuned` column, prepare the data by separating features and target, encode the target variable, and then split the data into training and testing sets for the cleaned dataset.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "249dd68e",
        "outputId": "7319279c-c468-489b-acb0-1a452b403152"
      },
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Identify anomalies in df_scaled and create df_cleaned\n",
        "# Anomalies are labeled as -1 by DBSCAN\n",
        "df_cleaned = df_scaled[df_scaled['dbscan_label_tuned'] != -1].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Original DataFrame size: {len(df_scaled)} rows\")\n",
        "print(f\"Cleaned DataFrame size (after removing anomalies): {len(df_cleaned)} rows\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Prepare data for the cleaned dataset\n",
        "# Features are the scaled numerical air quality metrics\n",
        "X_cleaned = df_cleaned[numerical_cols]\n",
        "# Target variable is the pollution category\n",
        "y_cleaned = df_cleaned['pollution_category']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Encode y_cleaned using the previously fitted label_encoder\n",
        "# It's important to use the same encoder to maintain consistent labels\n",
        "y_cleaned_encoded = label_encoder.transform(y_cleaned)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Original pollution categories in cleaned data:\", y_cleaned.unique())\n",
        "print(\"Encoded pollution labels in cleaned data (first 5):\", y_cleaned_encoded[:5])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Split X_cleaned and y_cleaned_encoded into new training and testing sets\n",
        "X_train_cleaned, X_test_cleaned, y_train_cleaned, y_test_cleaned = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X_cleaned, y_cleaned_encoded, test_size=0.2, random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nShape of X_train_cleaned: {X_train_cleaned.shape}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Shape of X_test_cleaned: {X_test_cleaned.shape}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Shape of y_train_cleaned: {y_train_cleaned.shape}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Shape of y_test_cleaned: {y_test_cleaned.shape}\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 19,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Original DataFrame size: 100 rows\n",
            "Cleaned DataFrame size (after removing anomalies): 56 rows\n",
            "\n",
            "Original pollution categories in cleaned data: ['Low' 'High' 'Moderate']\n",
            "Encoded pollution labels in cleaned data (first 5): [1 0 2 0 0]\n",
            "\n",
            "Shape of X_train_cleaned: (44, 6)\n",
